# Non-Nix pins (template authors)

One catalog: `modules/non-nix/catalog.json`. CLI tools install via mise (or
Nix when `versionAtLeast` + homepage identity match). Docker images and the
devenv VS Code extension share the same catalog but are not mise `[tools]`.

```
# ❌ BAD — consumers "upgrade" by editing generated mise.toml or HM wrappers
# home/llm-context.nix
serenaVersion = "1.8.0";

# ✅ GOOD — bump the catalog pin; `update` runs includes/update/non-nix.sh
# modules/non-nix/catalog.json  →  "name": "serena", "pin": "1.7.0"
```

`update` in this checkout runs those refreshers. It does not run
`devenv update` or `refresh-toolchain-latest`. Copier excludes this rule.
Do not edit `home/*-pkg.nix` (removed) or invent per-tool refreshers.
